  {
   "id": "jory",
   "name": "Jory Pell",
   "title": "Eel-Catcher of Kesselhaven",
   "hint": "a gnarled old man mending eel-traps",
   "meet": "The old eel-man spits, wipes his hand and holds it out. “Jory. Fifty years on this mole. You set a trap like a drunk priest, but you keep at it. I respect that.”",
   "talk": [
    "Jory tells you the harbour was twice as deep when he was a boy, and the eels twice as long.",
    "“Never eat an eel you didn’t kill yourself,” Jory says, and will not explain."
   ],
